---
title: "Link & reactive-input diagnostics"
---

This document deliberately trips the static `taliesin check` rules for broken relative
links and dangling/cyclic `{js}` reactive inputs. It lives in
`corpus/diagnostics/`, which is exempt from the corpus clean-render guards. Each located
finding jumps to its source line on click, like any other diagnostic.

## Broken relative links

A [link to a missing doc](no-such-doc.tmd) and a [link to a missing page](sub/gone.html)
both point at files that do not exist beside this document.

An [external link](https://example.com/anything) is never fetched, so it is left alone,
and an [in-page anchor](#broken-relative-links) to a real heading on this page is fine.

## Dangling and cyclic reactive inputs

A `{js}` cell consuming an input that nothing defines:

```{js}
//| input: undefined_name
return undefined_name;
```

A pair of `{js}` cells that depend on each other (a reactive dependency cycle):

```{js}
//| name: ping
//| input: pong
return pong;
```

```{js}
//| name: pong
//| input: ping
return ping;
```
